# Topological publish order for the rust-platform-libs crates.
#
# This list is the single source of truth for the order in which
# `.github/workflows/publish.yml` publishes the workspace's crates to
# crates.io. The order MUST respect the dependency DAG (a crate may
# only be published after every `platform-*` dependency of its
# published form is already on the registry), MUST be deterministic
# (no parallel publishes; one at a time, so a partial failure leaves
# a coherent registry state), and MUST exclude `platform-arch-tests`
# (workspace-internal tooling, `publish = false`).
#
# A unit test in `platform-arch-tests` reads this file and asserts the
# order is consistent with the manifest DAG, so the workflow and the
# source of truth cannot drift silently.
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments; non-comment, non-blank lines
# are the ordered crate names.

# 1. Foundation, no platform-* deps.
platform-core

# 2. Foundation; depends on platform-core.
platform-contracts

# 3. Foundation; depends on platform-core + platform-contracts.
platform-identity

# 4. Foundation; depends on platform-core + platform-contracts + platform-identity.
platform-audit

# 5. Public test-only support crate; depends on the four foundation
#    crates. Published so consumers can `cargo add --dev platform-testing`.
platform-testing

# 6. Satellite; depends on platform-core.
platform-mailing

# 7. Satellite; depends on platform-core.
platform-ai
